From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hao Li <hao.x.li@intel.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 13:05:54 -0700
Subject: Split buffer<->texture copies to work around Intel row-pitch
 limitation

Intel GPUs store a buffer<->texture copy's bytes per row in an 18-bit
hardware register (a row pitch of 262,144 bytes) and texels per row in
a separate 14-bit hardware register (a row width of 16,384 texels), so
a larger bytesPerRow silently overflows and corrupts the copy. Add a
workaround for Intel GPUs that splits affected buffer-to-texture and
texture-to-buffer copies on D3D11/D3D12/Vulkan into one command per row
so the oversized bytes and texels is never handed to the driver.

Bug: 481934465

Change-Id: Ib3e25be11f03d3f55205a3803dbbdb1817b9f7cb
Reviewed-on: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/336315
Commit-Queue: Corentin Wallez <cwallez@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Corentin Wallez <cwallez@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Loko Kung <lokokung@google.com>

